class StrictRiverSlopeTest{public static void main(String[]a){int n=96;float[] h=new float[n*n];for(int z=0;z<n;z++)for(int x=0;x<n;x++)h[z*n+x]=(float)(62+z*.07+Math.max(0,Math.abs(x-48)-5)*.55);var e=new EnvironmentMap(h);var r=RiverCourse.route(h,e,n,n,62,()->false,false,1,91,.1);int gentle=0,steep=0;for(int z=1;z<n-1;z++)for(int x=1;x<n-1;x++){int i=z*n+x;if(h[i]<=62)continue;double slope=RiverCourse.terrainSlope(h,n,x,z,1);if(slope>.1){steep++;if(r.flow().parent()[i]>=0)throw new AssertionError("Route enters steep sidehill");}else if(r.flow().parent()[i]>=0)gentle++;}if(steep<100||gentle<100)throw new AssertionError("Missing slope coverage");double[] safe=NaturalRivers.safe(30,50,new double[]{48,50},h,h,n,true);if(safe[0]!=48)throw new AssertionError("Rounded curve cuts into mountain");System.out.println("PASS: gentle valley routes="+gentle+" steep hillside cells excluded="+steep+"; curve displacement cannot cut uphill");}}
